 d the world as The Tallest Man on Earth\, Matsson has captivated audiences
  using\, as The New York Times describes\, “every inch of his long guita
 r cord to roam the stage: darting around\, crouching\, stretching\, hip-tw
 itching\, perching briefly and jittering away…Mr. Matsson is a guitar-sl
 inger rooted in folk\, and his songs are troubadour ballads at heart.”\n
